Best Claude Code workflow for the exercise

Give Claude Code prompts in this order:

1. Inspect first

> Inspect the Excel dataset in the project. Identify the sheet names, columns, data types, missing values, and potential fields that can be used to calculate shipment risk. Do not write the application yet.



2. Design

> Based on the actual dataset, propose a simple transparent risk-scoring methodology. Do not invent columns. Explain your assumptions and risk thresholds.



3. Build

> Build the Streamlit Pharma Shipment Risk Analyzer according to CLAUDE.md and the approved risk methodology. Keep data processing separate from the UI.



4. Test

> Run the application checks and test it against the supplied Excel file. Fix any column, type, missing-value, or UI issues you find.



